KNOWNBUG: \exists in JML preconditions / postconditions.

Sibling of jml-forall: the parser builds exists_exprt nodes,
but symex doesn't currently bind the quantifier variable. The
failure mode is identical:

    Invariant check failed
    Condition: found_l0
    Reason: level0: failed to find i

A skolemization pass that turns `\exists v. P(v)` into
`P(witness_v)` (where `witness_v` is a nondet int constrained
by the range) would unblock this. See jml-forall for the
broader options.
